WEBVTT

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:27.270
<i>The year is 1889.</i>

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:30.650
<i>The Nautilus is led into a trap set by Gargoyle,</i>

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.150
<i>and becomes the target of shelling by the American Fleet.</i>

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:37.700
<i>The Nautilus manages to escape, but the hull sustains heavy damage.</i>

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:41.910
<i>Lethal gas pours from a ruptured pipeline into the engine room.</i>

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.000
<i>To save the ship, Nemo seals off the room, trapping three crewmen.</i>

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.080
<i>The three eventually die to the horror of Jean,</i>

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.710
<i>and Nadia learns of the inhumanly unbending character of Nemo.</i>

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.210
<i>Jean realizes that science can also take human lives,</i>

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:56.670
<i>and that the Nautilus is engaged in a deadly war.</i>

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:28.210
Gargoyle not only wants to sink this ship,

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:32.170
but he also wants to get his hands on the Blue Water.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:36.210
It's the Blue Water that's causing all this trouble.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:40.930
It's the reason why so many people are dead!

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:44.390
Is the Nautilus so important?

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.770
Is the Blue Water that important?

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.020
It is.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:54.900
The Blue Water must be protected even if we lose everything else.

00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:00.530
That is the destiny of those who possess the Blue Water.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:14.210
If it's going to cause me so much anguish, I don't want it anymore!

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:22.640
I mustn't!

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.570
As you are all aware,

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:49.330
in our last battle we lost three of our comrades in the engine crew.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:54.960
We have brought their remains here to their homeland.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:04:01.050
We shall now proceed to the Sunken Cathedral in the Natal Sea Valley.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.470
Prepare to dive!

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:18.360
Please save me! Won't someone come and save me? Please...

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.860
Jean...

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:25.280
What is it?

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:27.740
Could you look up something for me?

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:33.920
How is it?

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:38.040
Well, no matter how much I increase magnification,

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:45.010
the designs are still there in three dimensions.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.300
I wonder what these designs mean?

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.730
What is that?

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.810
An armor plate from the Nautilus.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:59.770
It's supposed to be the hardest metal in the world.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:09.530
Incredible! It produced scratches on the plate.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:16.250
How can it be so hard? What can the Blue Water be made of?

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.080
I'm sorry,

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:21.840
but the composition of this stone is far beyond my ability to determine.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:26.800
I see. Thanks anyway, Jean.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.010
I'm really sorry.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.060
No, it's okay.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.600
I wonder why I have this stone?

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:43.230
Can this be what they call destiny?

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:50.280
That's right. Fait and the others gave their lives to save ours.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:56.750
That was their destiny as written in the stars.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:01.170
You mean they had to die even if they wanted to live?

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:04.010
Yes.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.130
Then the fact that they died,

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.300
and the fact that we're on this ship,

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:15.140
and the reason I have the Blue Water, the very cause of all this warfare,

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:17.180
is a matter of destiny?

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:25.570
Of course. That is the destiny you were born with.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:28.950
No...

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.530
Then, what is the reason I was born?

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:37.500
To discover that very reason.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:45.960
To live from day to day with such thoughts?

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.010
Is that the destiny of those possessing the Blue Water?

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:05.610
Did you come to see me?

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:12.320
All right. Come in.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.290
Please tell me one thing.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.460
Why did Mr. Fait die?

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.420
Because of me.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.400
You were keeping watch?

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:47.320
Yes, there were so many things I still wanted to teach them.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:33.570
Why? All of us have died!

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:34.610
You murderer!

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:35.870
Why?

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:38.080
Why did we die?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:41.330
Why? Why are you alive?

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.080
Why? Why?

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:46.210
Why you? Why?

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:47.750
Why?

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:50.090
How can you go on living?

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:05.350
Are you an adventurer who is

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:10.570
prepared to climb the waterfall named Perilous,

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:14.400
and seek the truth of the legend that lies therein?

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.450
Then you must first seek me!

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:28.520
All crew members will prepare for the funeral. We have landed in Atlantis.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:30.900
Atlantis?

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:14.440
Isn't it exciting that such a place exists at the bottom of the sea?

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:36.880
Atlantis, the legendary continent that was destroyed 12,000 years ago.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:41.510
There's nothing left alive. It's a world of death and silence.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:46.890
Atlantis... I wonder what caused its destruction?

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:53.980
I wonder? These pebbles are glass,

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:57.690
and they are all uniformly round.

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:03.610
I know! They were created under the pressure of terrific heat!

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:09.160
Exactly! It was hot enough to melt stones.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:14.580
It was the power of that crystal tower we came down, the Tower of Babel.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.040
What?

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:19.840
Gargoyle tried to construct a similar tower, but failed.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:24.470
This is the original tower. Never again will it show its dreadful power.

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:29.310
Actually, it wasn't meant to be used as a destructive weapon.

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:31.430
Then what was its real purpose?

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:49.870
These are...

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:51.000
...gravestones.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:53.830
Gravestones? How do you know?

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:55.710
I can't say.

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:59.000
We call it the Sunken Cathedral.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:03.170
This place was not originally built as a cemetery.

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:09.140
A long time ago, a great number of Atlantis citizens died here.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:12.980
This area was used as a temporary cemetery for the people

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:16.400
until they could return to their homeland.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:21.860
All of those who perish in our war against Gargoyle sleep here.

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:27.700
Atlantis... Neo Atlantis... Blue Water...

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:33.830
No, I hate it! I don't want to listen to such stories anymore!

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.170
Let's go.

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.970
The sonar officer! Why are you praying here?

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:55.640
Just a moment.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:59.810
They used to be comrades of mine.

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:10.200
I wish I could have brought you some French wine. I'm sorry.

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:12.490
French?

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:17.000
That's right. My real name is Eiko Villan. I'm French.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:18.960
I can't believe it!

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:22.420
Mr. Eiko, what was the name of your ship?

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:27.380
The Elyse out of Le Havre. We were sunk by the Garfish.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:31.800
I was the only one saved by the Nautilus.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:34.430
What was the captain's name?

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:39.020
Captain Raltique... Rocque Raltique.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:42.060
He was a fine man.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:48.450
Father...

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:42.790
Captain Nemo, may I ask you one more question?

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:47.420
How...

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:52.340
How can you go on living after causing all of these people's deaths?

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:57.100
Please answer me!

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.980
Eventually, I will die too.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:07.690
But before that happens, there is a mission I must accomplish.

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:20.410
Captain!

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:27.380
People who sin must be punished according to the gravity of their sins.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:31.880
The Captain is carrying a heavy cross.

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:36.800
He has to continue living for the sake of all those who have died,

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:40.390
to achieve a mission that must be accomplished.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:44.100
You will understand when the time comes.

00:16:54.910 --> 00:17:00.120
If the captain's punishment for his sins is meeting Nadia again,

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.160
there can be nothing more cruel.

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:33.070
They're real flowers!

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:54.630
Jean!

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:04.180
Water?

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:52.480
Even people with the knowledge to construct such marvelous things

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:55.110
must in time die off and disappear.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:18.220
Jean!

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:37.980
You told me once how you were going to build your own airplane.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:42.530
That was before. It doesn't matter anymore.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:48.080
Even if I sail all over the seven seas,

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:52.500
or search the heavens above, I know I won't find my father.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:06.180
Inventions are made to bring happiness, aren't they?

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:09.180
Jean...

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:13.770
Do you remember how it was when we first met?

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:19.740
At that time, you told me that we have only one life to live.

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:25.740
Let's make it a bright and happy one.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:30.370
That's not it! We've got to make the most of it!

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:36.630
It was my uncle who said that. They were his favorite words.

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:41.300
He was a nice person.

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:44.760
Jean?

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:45.470
Yes?

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:47.850
Do you want to go home to Le Havre?

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.140
No.

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:53.890
You mean you want to board that ship again?

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:54.900
Yes.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:56.350
Why?

00:20:58.570 --> 00:21:02.280
Because I want to become friends with all the people on board the Nautilus.

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:06.070
That's right, I like them very much.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.460
Let's go.

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:20.500
Back to where everybody is.

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:25.050
All right.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:34.230
It's amazing how it can blossom in a place like this.

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:40.400
It's beautiful, much prettier than the ones Gargoyle made.

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:45.610
Nadia!

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:48.490
Should you?

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:51.240
Yes, I understand now.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.790
I realize that I must pick this flower.

00:22:10.390 --> 00:22:15.020
See this flower in the Darkness, and know the Joy of Life.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:17.230
This flower is verily the Force of Life.

00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:23.610
Learn awe of the Darkness. Close your eyes and think of the Darkness.

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:28.150
Darkness is the Lord of Unease. Darkness is verily the Kingdom of Death.

00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:31.160
Do not forget Darkness when there is Light.

00:22:31.160 --> 00:22:33.660
Do not forget the flower when there is Darkness.

00:22:33.660 --> 00:22:35.790
Do not forget the unmerciful and unfeeling nature

00:22:35.790 --> 00:22:38.120
when you look into the Darkness within your hearts.

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:43.500
Be in awe of the Darkness. Close your eyes and think of the Darkness.

00:22:44.090 --> 00:22:48.220
We say unto you, rest in unbroken sleep

00:22:48.220 --> 00:22:50.550
until the day when we return to our home beyond the stars.

00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:57.520
From this day, we become inhabitants of the Darkness. Each of us

00:22:57.980 --> 00:23:03.480
offers flowers, and an uneasy peace within our hearts.

00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:12.410
Farewell...
